# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# BELT AND BRACES (added with the D26 pre-git safety mechanism)
#
# Everything above is the policy. This block is the rest of the denylist, and
# `.githooks/check-denylist.mjs` is the mechanism that catches what BOTH miss — a `git add -f`,
# or an extension nobody thought of. The three are meant to agree; if you change one, change
# the others. The full ruling on what may live in git is ASSET-PROVENANCE.md.
#
#   git config core.hooksPath .githooks     <- one command per clone; `pnpm install` does it
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

