# ── Adding an exception ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A `!` line here is not enough on its own: the pre-commit hook and the CI job read their own
# allowlist. To genuinely permit a file you must do all three, deliberately:
#   1. add the `!` line here,
#   2. add it to PATH_ALLOW (or SIZE_ALLOW) in .githooks/check-denylist.mjs, WITH A REASON,
#   3. record the ruling and its evidence in ASSET-PROVENANCE.md.
# One file at a time. Never a whole directory.

# Oracle sweeps: per-chunk statistics decoded from the 2016 baked terrain.
# Derived from World Machine output whose licence question is still open
# (content/MANIFEST.md, D26), so they stay local. Regenerate with
# `pnpm oracle:sweep` — it needs the legacy Unity project mounted.
tools/terrain/.oracle/
test-results/
route-sweep-out/

# `tests/e2e/perf-trace.spec.ts`'s output (VR-PERF §5.9 H3): a summary and a
# per-frame CSV, a few hundred kB a run. It is deliberately NOT under
# `test-results/`, which Playwright wipes at the start of every run — a trace
# you wanted to compare against the next one would lose its first half.
# Overridable with PERF_TRACE_DIR; the default is ignored here.
perf-out/

# `tests/e2e/title-foreground.spec.ts`'s census (DEV-287): every prop in the
# title frame, ranked by the pixels it covers, with the mesh-space coordinate
# to paste into `content/no-prop-volumes.json`. A MEASUREMENT of one build on
# one viewport, so committing it would be committing a number that is stale the
# next time the scatter or the camera moves. Overridable with
# TITLE_CENSUS_OUT; the default is ignored here.
/title-foreground-census.json

# Throwaway diagnostic specs. A probe reads the session scratchpad by absolute
# path and dies with the session, so committing one leaves a permanently broken
# test that also names a home directory (PUBLIC-CHECKLIST Gate 4). Name a
# scratch spec with a LEADING UNDERSCORE and it cannot be committed by accident
# — `tests/unit/legacy-root.test.ts`'s gate skips it for the same reason.
#
# The pattern is the whole `_` prefix rather than `_probe*` because three
# different names turned up in one day (`_probe2`, `zz-probe`, `_measure-orbs`)
# and the narrow rule missed them one at a time. FOUR spellings turned up in two
# days -- `_probe2.test.ts`, `zz-probe.spec.ts`, `_measure-orbs.test.ts`,
# `zz-probe-dev061.test.ts` -- and each time the rule was widened to the one
# just seen rather than to the CLASS, so it missed the next one. Both prefixes,
# both extensions, done. No tracked test in this repo starts with `_` or `zz-`;
# checked, 118 files.
tests/**/_*.test.ts
tests/**/_*.spec.ts
tests/**/zz-*.test.ts
tests/**/zz-*.spec.ts

# Manifest fragment from tools/assets/extract-props.mjs. A merge aid, not source.
tools/assets/props-rows.json

# World Machine density maps. Regenerable from $FF2_LEGACY, never published:
# the scatter is baked into content/environments/*.json (O13 / C-6).
tools/assets/.density/

# ── CARRIED, NEVER COMMITTED ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Written by `tools/release/copy-list.mjs`. These files are ON DISK because the
# work needs them — `pnpm extract` cannot run without the guid index — and OUT
# of git because this repository will one day be made public, and flipping a
# repo flips its whole history.
#
# Tracking one of these with a promise to remove it later is the promise that
# made a fresh repository necessary in the first place (D33).

/PUBLIC-CHECKLIST.md
/docs/research/08-third-party-audit.md
/docs/research/_guid_index.tsv
/docs/research/_script_guids_topic03.tsv
/docs/research/_verify-v-meta-3p.md

# The GPU lease (tools/agent/gpu.sh) is a directory made with mkdir, held for
# minutes at a time; it is state, never content.
tools/agent/gpu.lock/
tools/agent/gpu.queue/

# Local Cloudflare Pages Functions secrets (wrangler pages dev). Never committed:
# production values live only in Cloudflare (PLAYER-GHOSTS.md, DEV-372).
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*

# Wrangler's local state (`wrangler pages dev`, `wrangler d1 ... --local`): the LOCAL D1
# SQLite files and caches. Machine state, never content (docs/lap-server.md, DEV-372).
.wrangler/

# Content pack output (pnpm content:pack). Never committed.
/content-pack/
# A dry-run export of the public facetedflight tree (tools/release/export-public.mjs).
/.export-dry*
